The new advertisement workflow fails for its documented non-contiguous block selection, and two helper scripts fail or crash in common cache/font conditions.

Full review comments:

- [P1] Handle separators when finding the next segment boundary — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\pub.py:142-144
  When the selected blocks contain multiple non-contiguous segments, such as the documented `0,1,2,8,9`, `z` points to the space between blocks. Passing `z, z + 1` to `lettres` therefore finds no alphanumeric character and raises `IndexError`, so `pub.py` cannot create the advertisement.

- [P2] Use a font available in the repository — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\proto_inserts.py:67-67
  On a normal checkout, `arial.ttf` is not in the working directory and Pillow does not resolve a bare filename through `C:\Windows\Fonts`, so every `proto_inserts.py` run reaches this line and fails with `OSError: cannot open resource`. Use the repository font or the existing font helper instead.

- [P2] Require the alignment JSON before reading it — C:\Users\NR SMART\tools\lcdg-reel\scripts\controle_voix.py:49-52
  If a narration cache is interrupted after the MP3 is written but before its alignment JSON is written, this check passes and the next line raises an unhandled `FileNotFoundError`. Treat the cache as missing unless both `mp3` and `js` exist, matching `voix.synthese`'s cache behavior.
